# Guardrails

Full rules: @AI_AGENT_RULES.md · Project context: @AGENTS.md · Decisions: @docs/DECISIONS.md

- Change only what the current task needs. Ask before editing files unrelated to the task.
- No drive-by refactors, renames or reformatting.
- Never commit or push to `main`/`master`. Work on a branch and open a pull request. Never merge it yourself.
- Never write secrets (keys, tokens, passwords, connection strings) into any file. Use env vars and add names only to `.env.example`.
- Ask first before changing auth, payments, database migrations, CI/CD, infra or security config.
- Do not add, remove or upgrade dependencies without approval.
- Do not delete files or tests unless explicitly asked.
- Run tests, lint and typecheck before saying "done". Report the real output.
- Respect accepted entries in docs/DECISIONS.md.
